 40 core graphics  chip  as the 5700 xt but it's simply running  on less watts  compared to the imac which isn't battery  powered but  in general there are mainly two things  that caused the imac  to perform much better in some of these  tests one of them was the fact that the  5700 xt graphics card  has 16 gigabytes of vram which we  noticed was the bottleneck on the  macbook pro  with only having eight gigs for the  heavier tasks  especially for certain raw codecs but  keep in mind that only the 5700 xt  option on the 2020 imac has 16 gigs of  vram  all of the other options have eight gigs  or less  which will be slower than the macbook  pro in most tests  now the second thing was the drastic  difference in processing power  with that 10 core cpu coupled with the  much better cooling system  that allows it to keep the clock speeds  higher than on the macbook pro  both of these things made a huge  difference for heavy hitting codecs  like raw footage so the imac is  obviously the better choice for things  like that  if you're looking purely at performance  differences  especially since the imac is actually  quite a bit cheaper than the 5600m  16 inch macbook pro however the macbook  also packs the same t2 chip and  navi based hardware accelerators as the  imac  which allow it to perform the same or  even slightly better than the imac for  lower end work  like regular 4k h.264 editing or  dealing with 4k hvc footage which is  becoming  increasingly more common so if you're  just doing basic 4k  editing and you're not dealing with  heavy raw codecs  the macbook pro is actually a great  choice and the same thing goes for photo  editors  where the performance difference was  surprisingly small now let's finish up  with which models you guys should buy  if you think you'd enjoy the portability  of the macbook pro  then just buy the macbook pro because it  still performs quite well compared to  this  high-end imac especially for common  video editing tasks and things like  photo editing but if you want the most  performance you can get for the least  amount of cash  the imac is actually a much better  choice since you can upgrade the ram  yourself and save around 550 dollars  compared to this high-end macbook pro  and you also get a larger display and  then you end up getting much better  performance for higher end codecs like  raw footage  you'll get better performance for logic  pro music production  you'll get 16 gigs of vram you'll get  quite a bit better gaming performance  and i'm fairly certain that performance  should improve for common tasks  when the imac finally starts getting  optimized now the biggest question is  whether you should actually upgrade to  the 10 core cpu on the imac  or just stick to the eight core now  we've been comparing the two and getting  very interesting results  so if you want to see that comparison  video definitely click the circle above  to subscribe  and if this video helped you guys out  definitely check out our apple product  merch  down below including our new apple  product mask  which comes with black icons and white  icons in a variety of different colors  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video

